## Experimental design
1.   Sample size
Describe how sample size was determined.
No sample size calculation was performed prior to  recruitment of patients. The current sample size was considered suficient as it allowed to detect a minimum difference of B2 enterotype prevalence between mHC $(n=66$ and the smallest PSC patient group $\left(\mathsf{n}{=}18\right)$ of $34.3\%$ as significant (assuming $a=0.05$ , $\scriptstyle\beta=0.2^{\prime}$ ).
2.   Data exclusions Describe any data exclusions.
3.   Replication
Describe whether the experimental findings were reliably reproduced.
Findings were replicated in the Flemish Gut Flora population cohort $(N{=}1106)$ when concerning available variables as reported in the manuscript. Disease-specific near-exclusion patterns were replicated in an independent dataset. Two of the taxon-taxon associations were not reproduced in the validation dataset as reported in the manuscript.
4.   Randomization
Describe how samples/organisms/participants were allocated into experimental groups.
Not applicable, as this was not a randomized study. This was a case-control study where controls were matched to patients with PSC on age, gender, and body mass index. For a complete description of the cohort reanalyzed in this study, we refer to the original publication (doi: 10.1136/gutjnl-2015-311004).
5.   Blinding
Describe whether the investigators were blinded to group allocation during data collection and/or analysis.
The present study is a QMP-based reanalysis of an explorative cohort study. Patients were included based on diagnosis. Investigators were not blinded during data collection or analyses.
