## Software
## Policy information about availability of computer code
7. Software
Describe the software used to analyze the data in this study.
16S sequencing data pre-processing for the study cohort was performed using FLASH software v1.2.10 for paired-end reads merging, USEARCH (version 9.2.64) was used for quality filtering and for chimera removal. For the validation cohort, the DADA2 pipeline (version 1.6.0) was used for these tasks Taxonomy assignment for both datasets was done using the RDP classifier (version 2.12). Quantitative microbiome profiles (QMP) were computed from 16S sequencing data and faecal cell density values using the custom R code provided by the authors. The code (R) used to compute quantitative microbiome profiles (QMP) can be found at https:// github.com/raeslab/QMP/. BD Accuri CFlow software was used to gate and separate the microbial fluorescence events to measure faecal microbial cell densities by flow cytometry. Data analysis and graphical representations were performed using ${\sf R},$ a free software environment for statistical computing (packages used are detailed in methods).
For manuscripts utilizing custom algorithms or software that are central to the paper but not yet described in the published literature, software must be made available to editors and reviewers upon request. We strongly encourage code deposition in a community repository (e.g. GitHub). Nature Methods guidance for providing algorithms and software for publication provides further information on this topic.
